\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces End-to-end system architecture showing the three parallel detection pathways and their integration. Input frames pass through a single preprocessing routine---resize to $224\times 224$ followed by ImageNet normalization---that is shared byte-for-byte with the routine used when the memory banks and autoencoder were fit. The three detectors emit raw anomaly scores that are standardized to a common z-score scale and fused by weighted averaging.}}{3}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{2}{3}{End-to-end system architecture showing the three parallel detection pathways and their integration. Input frames pass through a single preprocessing routine---resize to $224\times 224$ followed by ImageNet normalization---that is shared byte-for-byte with the routine used when the memory banks and autoencoder were fit. The three detectors emit raw anomaly scores that are standardized to a common z-score scale and fused by weighted averaging}{figure.caption.2}{}}
